  - THREE THINGS VARY BY SEX AND STAGE and are stored in two places. The sex''s automatic skills are the `male` and `female` variants (skills_additional). The stage is a pick-one group of four named abilities, each naming its sex; the rogue options carry the printed additions as bonuses, restate the Horror Factor and name the O.C.C.s. Nothing ties the variant to the stage pick: a male variant with a female stage is the player''s error to avoid.
  - Skills, catalog base plus printed bonus: Horsemanship: Exotic (+30%, 30+30=60, catalog name Horsemanship: Exotic Animals) for all; males Wilderness Survival (+20%, 50), Land Navigation (+15%, 51), Dowsing (+15%, 35), Track and Trap Animals (+15%, 35); females First Aid (+20%, 65), Cook (+20%, 55), Sewing (+10%, 50), Sing (+10%, 45), Skin and Prepare Animal Hides (+15%, 45). Printed 34 says the youngling skills "only now increase with true experience" once an O.C.C. is taken; per_level is stored at the catalog figure and that sentence is in the Male Rogue text.
  - Languages prints "Dragonese/Elven" with no percentage; stored as Language: Dragonese at 98, the native-tongue figure. No literacy is printed and none is stored.
  - Attacks Per Melee prints "Two or three as a simple hunter or by O.C.C. At rogue stage, three melee attacks plus those gained by hand to hand combat skills and experience." Stored as combat.attacks_base 2 on the race (the lower printed figure) and combat.attacks 3 on each rogue option, with the sentence kept in natural_abilities.
  - Male Rogue (printed 34): added dice I.Q. 2D6, M.E. 2D6, M.A. 1D6, P.S. 2D6, P.P. 1D6, P.E. 2D6, P.B. 0, Spd 1D6; Hit Points add 10; S.D.C. add 2D4x10; weight add 2D4x10 lbs; A.R. 12; Horror Factor 14; P.P.E. add 2D6. "Any are available except Psychics", so occ_options lists every non-psychic Palladium Fantasy O.C.C. the catalog holds; a later import is not covered until added.
  - Female Rogue (printed 35): added dice I.Q. 2D6, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 0, P.P. 0, P.E. 1D6, P.B. 0, Spd 0; Hit Points add 10; S.D.C. add 1D6x10; weight add 6D6x10 lbs; A.R. 12; Horror Factor 15; P.P.E. add 1D6x10. "Eandroth Mind Mage O.C.C. Only! ... Use the Mind Mage experience table." Her printed I.S.P. (2D6x10+140, +10 per level) differs from the Mind Mage O.C.C.''s own figure and is stored as prose in the option''s description.
  - Psionics (printed 33): "Prior to this, they possess 2D6x10 P.P.E., 4D6 I.S.P. and the psionic power to Sense Evil." The 4D6 I.S.P. and Sense Evil are a psionics block on the Young Female option; the page names no tier and "minor" is the label chosen for one power. The 2D6x10 P.P.E. disagrees with the Average P.P.E. line (2D6) on the same page; ppe_base stays 2D6 and the larger figure is prose in the option.
  - The page prints no Psionics line for males. psionics_allowed is not stated.
  - The psionic heat point is a natural power with no I.S.P. cost, printed 33-34; stored as prose in natural_abilities.
  - Printed 215 says Eandroth use the experience table of their chosen O.C.C., so no xp_table is stored.
  - The entry prints no money and no equipment line; none is stored. The rogue''s favored double-bladed knife (2D4) is a preference, not a grant.
  - Size 4 and a half to 5 feet (1.4 to 1.5 m), 75-135 lbs; life span 25-30 years when young, 350 for a male rogue, up to 500 for a female. In the Lore.
