## Lore

The Eandroth are small reptilian humanoids with fine scales and a tail, built something like an upright hunting dinosaur. Nobody knows where they came from; a magical experiment and a summoning from another world are the usual guesses. For their first twenty-four years they are slight and smooth-skinned, with an open, cheerful nature that deserts them only in the twice-yearly mating season, when the males fight brutal ritual duels for the few females.

They are desert nomads. Tribes are usually under fifty strong, but caravans range from a dozen riders to many hundreds, with herds of Silonar and Drayback lizards, wagons and a matriarch at the center. Every Eandroth rides the two-legged Silonar from childhood and will use the animal as a weapon. A big caravan is strong enough that raiders leave it alone, which often makes it the nearest thing to law for miles around, and travelers who deal fairly can count on a welcome and on a chance to trade for food, gear and weapons.

Those who live long enough change. A male who survives some fifty mating seasons, or a female who has borne young twenty-five times or more, becomes a rogue: a larger, harder and cleverer creature in a slack, creased hide, with none of the old gentleness left. Male rogues leave to wander the world for a century or so, learning a profession, before many return to lead and teach their tribes in war. Female rogues are far rarer. They grow enormously heavy, their minds open into great psionic power, and they are the real rulers of their people, fiercely protective and terrible when a friend is harmed.

**Alignment:** Any; the young are usually anarchist or unprincipled, and rogues are mostly good.

**O.C.C.s available:** None before the age of 25. A male rogue takes any except a psychic class, most often a man of arms, a cleric or a scholar. A female rogue is a Mind Mage.

**Size:** 4 and a half to 5 feet (1.4 to 1.5 m). **Weight:** 75-135 lbs; a male rogue adds 2D4x10 lbs and a female rogue 6D6x10 lbs.

**Average Life Span:** 25-30 years; a male rogue may reach 350 and a female rogue 500.

**Habitat:** Extreme desert and hot grassland, chiefly the Baalgor Wastelands and parts of the Old Kingdom; one tribe has moved to the Land of the South-Winds. Rogues wander almost anywhere that is not cold.

**Enemies and Allies:** None as such, though they are a wary people.

## GM Notes

A player Eandroth is one of four things, and the choice sets the whole character: a young male or female with no O.C.C. and only the tribe''s hunting or camp skills, or a rogue of either sex who starts a first-level O.C.C. with the rogue''s larger attributes. The sex is chosen as the variant and the stage as the special ability; keep the two in agreement.

The heat point is slow and easy to break. It needs 1D6 minutes of stillness and a target that does not move, and the victim feels feverish before he drops, which warns anyone who knows the Eandroth. Its real danger is a large group using it together.

Male rogues seldom wear armor except for a planned battle, then scale or splint, and favor knives and swords. During the wandering years they avoid their own kind and are short with them. Roughly a third of males and half of females live to become rogues.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'eandroth');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'eandroth';

